<header><p class="st-kicker">colony · Mesoamerica and the Caribbean</p><h1 class="st-title">Colony of the Bay Islands</h1><p class="st-meta">1852 CE – 1860 CE · capital Coxen Hole</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Brief British colony on Roatán and the neighbouring islands off Honduras, whose creation clashed with a treaty with the United States.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>From the 1830s English-speaking settlers, many from the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/cayman-islands">Cayman Islands</a> and other British <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caribbean">Caribbean</a> islands, settled on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/roatan">Roatán</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/utila">Utila</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guanaja">Guanaja</a>, where <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/garifuna">Garifuna</a> communities already lived. The superintendent of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/belize">Belize</a> claimed the islands for <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/united-kingdom">Britain</a>, and in 1852 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a> proclaimed them the Colony of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bay-islands">Bay Islands</a>, under the oversight of the Jamaican governor.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The colony was small, with a few thousand inhabitants living by fishing, turtling, coconuts and fruit trade with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-orleans">New Orleans</a>, and was run by a lieutenant governor and local council at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/coxen-hole">Coxen Hole</a>. The <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/united-states">United States</a> protested that the colony breached the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/clayton-bulwer-treaty">Clayton-Bulwer Treaty</a> of 1850, in which both powers had agreed not to colonise <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/central-america">Central America</a>. <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/republic-of-honduras">Honduras</a> also claimed the islands as its own.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Seeking better relations with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/washington-dc">Washington</a>, <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/united-kingdom">Britain</a> signed the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wyke-cruz-treaty">Wyke-Cruz Treaty</a> with <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/republic-of-honduras">Honduras</a> in 1859 and handed over the islands in 1860. Their English-speaking, largely Protestant population remained, and the islands are now a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/departement">department</a> of Honduras.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="colony, 1852 CE – 1860 CE"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M20 64 H80 L70 78 H30 Z"/><path d="M50 64 V18"/><path d="M50 22 L72 56 H50"/><path d="M50 28 L32 56 H50"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">colony</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Mesoamerica and the Caribbean</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:96.56%;width:1.20%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1852 CE – 1860 CE</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>colony</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>colonial</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Coxen Hole</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Protestantism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>English</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/honduras">Honduras</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Bay Islands</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1856&amp;focus=colony-of-the-bay-islands" aria-label="Colony of the Bay Islands on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="2323 1571 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Colony of the Bay Islands lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M2643 1827L4997 651M2643 1827L2626 1889"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M4997 651h0M2626 1889h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M2643 1827h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M2643 1827h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Coxen Hole. <a href="/atlas?year=1856&amp;focus=colony-of-the